(6092013, 895455, 118472, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by saxon75:</b></div><hr/><i> A parking lot seems like a great idea for potential chaos, but I don''t get much of a sense of that here.  As for the technical parts, the blown highlights in the sky are a problem, and the white balance appears to be off.  The angle is also kind of boring--a higher or lower angle would make this more interesting, instead of just taking it from a standing position as it appears you''ve done.  Main thing is to really think about what''s being included in the image and why. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Well, actually, I realized that I should have been more global in my subject. This event is well known where I live as something chaotic. It''s like a huge hippie party where there is a lot of people drunk and high, here to listen music shows lol I anticipated that everyone knows it but that''s not the fact. My mistake. Maybe I should have shot the part on the right of the coach to express my idea ( cars parked everywhere, through picnic tables, fire set and tents) The white balance was set but my adjustments f*** it up. I agree with you about the angle, but it''s not the kind of place where you can bring a ladder hahaha Just kidding ! Thanks for your comment ;)</td>', 'Originally posted by saxon75: A parking lot seems like a great idea for potential chaos, but I don''t get much of a sense of that here.  As for the technical parts, the blown highlights in the sky are a problem, and the white balance appears to be off.  The angle is also kind of boring--a higher or lower angle would make this more interesting, instead of just taking it from a standing position as it appears you''ve done.  Main thing is to really think about what''s being included in the image and why.   Well, actually, I realized that I should have been more global in my subject. This event is well known where I live as something chaotic. It''s like a huge hippie party where there is a lot of people drunk and high, here to listen music shows lol I anticipated that everyone knows it but that''s not the fact. My mistake. Maybe I should have shot the part on the right of the coach to express my idea ( cars parked everywhere, through picnic tables, fire set and tents) The white balance was set but my adjustments f*** it up. I agree with you about the angle, but it''s not the kind of place where you can bring a ladder hahaha Just kidding ! Thanks for your comment ;)', '2010-07-14 02:30:00.000000', NULL, 0),
